1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,924
The invitation arrived in the most old-fashioned way
available: a handwritten card, in

2
00:00:13,944 --> 00:00:20,140
English, delivered to the Singapore tower by a
member of the Chinese consular staff who

3
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,070
did not stay for an answer.

4
00:00:22,469 --> 00:00:29,044
It said: *Dr. Wesker. I have read everything you
have published in ten years. I would

5
00:00:29,064 --> 00:00:35,872
like to talk about the part you have not. Beihai
Park, the northern bench, 4 April, 6:40

6
00:00:35,892 --> 00:00:38,199
a.m. Come alone; I will. — W.*

7
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:44,447
Catherine called it a trap. Carrick called it a trap.
Sloane, who was told about it eleven

8
00:00:44,467 --> 00:00:50,511
days later and who had never been told anything before,
called it the single most interesting

9
00:00:50,531 --> 00:00:55,009
document to come out of the Ministry of
State Security in his career.

10
00:00:55,409 --> 00:01:01,430
Wesker went alone, on a Saturday morning, and sat
down on a stone bench beside a lake

11
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:06,120
with a woman in a dark coat who had
brought two paper cups of tea.

12
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,890
You are younger than the photographs.

13
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:13,300
The photographs are ten years old
and I have not aged.

14
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:17,430
Yes. That is the sixth item on my
list. We will come to it.

15
00:01:17,829 --> 00:01:23,585
Director Wen Shulan was fifty-eight, twenty-nine
years in the service, and she ran the

16
00:01:23,605 --> 00:01:29,428
directorate that had been watching Umbrella since
the Basel keynote. The narrator would

17
00:01:29,448 --> 00:01:35,338
like to record, at the start, that she was the only
person in the entire account who was

18
00:01:35,358 --> 00:01:40,980
never once wrong about Albert Wesker, and that she
never told anybody what she knew.

19
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:46,762
I am going to say six things. You will not confirm
any of them, and I do not need you

20
00:01:46,782 --> 00:01:52,106
to. Then I am going to make you an offer, and you
will accept it, because it is better

21
00:01:52,126 --> 00:01:57,388
than the alternative and because you have already
worked out what the alternative is.

22
00:01:57,789 --> 00:01:58,539
Please.

23
00:01:58,938 --> 00:02:04,822
One. Your buildings are not built. We have satellite
imagery of the Newark site from the

24
00:02:04,842 --> 00:02:10,658
eighth and the ninth of January 2027. I have looked
at those two images for nine years.

25
00:02:10,938 --> 00:02:16,591
Two. A proportion of your staff did not exist before
the day they were hired. We identified

26
00:02:16,611 --> 00:02:22,389
four hundred and eleven of them by the absence of
dental records. People have dental records,

27
00:02:22,409 --> 00:02:25,568
Dr. Wesker. Even poor people. Even
in your country.

28
00:02:25,848 --> 00:02:31,426
Three. Your organisation contained an outbreak in
sixty-one days using an antiviral which

29
00:02:31,446 --> 00:02:36,897
was designed, validated and manufactured in four.
That is not possible, and I mean that

30
00:02:36,917 --> 00:02:40,293
as a statement about chemistry, not
about your people.

31
00:02:40,574 --> 00:02:45,871
Four. The thing that walked into the stadium in Lyon
was not equipment. I have the thermal

32
00:02:45,891 --> 00:02:50,833
record from a French source. Its core temperature
was thirty-nine point two degrees.

33
00:02:51,114 --> 00:02:56,692
Five. You have no ambition that I can find, which
frightens me more than any of the others.

34
00:02:56,712 --> 00:03:02,230
Every powerful man I have studied wants something
specific and can be modelled. You appear

35
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:07,582
to want *more*, without a terminus, and a thing
without a terminus cannot be negotiated

36
00:03:07,602 --> 00:03:09,120
with in the ordinary way.

37
00:03:09,786 --> 00:03:11,495
Six. You are not from here.

38
00:03:11,895 --> 00:03:17,598
Wesker drank his tea, and the narrator notes that
this was the first time in ten years

39
00:03:17,618 --> 00:03:23,587
that anyone had put the sixth item on the table, and
that he had come to Beijing precisely

40
00:03:23,607 --> 00:03:28,045
because he had known, from the wording of
the card, that she would.

41
00:03:28,566 --> 00:03:29,995
Ask your question.

42
00:03:30,395 --> 00:03:35,597
I have no question. I have a country of one point four
billion people, and I am responsible

43
00:03:35,617 --> 00:03:40,531
for a small part of keeping it safe, and the only
relevant fact is that there is a man

44
00:03:40,551 --> 00:03:45,408
on this planet who can do things no state can do
and who has so far chosen to do good

45
00:03:45,428 --> 00:03:50,572
with them. My question would be *what are you*, and
you would lie, and we would both waste

46
00:03:50,592 --> 00:03:51,145
a morning.

47
00:03:51,425 --> 00:03:53,275
So instead: my offer.

48
00:03:53,675 --> 00:03:59,686
The offer took her four minutes and it was the most
sophisticated thing anybody ever put

49
00:03:59,706 --> 00:04:00,165
to him.

50
00:04:00,686 --> 00:04:05,850
You will build in China. Plants, laboratories, a
tower in Shanghai if you want one — and

51
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:10,976
you will build them the ordinary way, with
contractors, with permits, over three years,

52
00:04:10,996 --> 00:04:16,103
where our people can watch the concrete go in.
Everything you sell to our public health

53
00:04:16,123 --> 00:04:20,522
system will be manufactured in our territory
by people with dental records.

54
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:25,963
In exchange: nobody in this government will ever
look in your basement. No inspection,

55
00:04:25,983 --> 00:04:31,143
no investigation, no interest. If a provincial
official develops curiosity, he will be

56
00:04:31,163 --> 00:04:36,443
transferred. I will personally ensure that the word
*Umbrella* never appears in a threat

57
00:04:36,463 --> 00:04:38,793
assessment as long as I hold this desk.

58
00:04:39,192 --> 00:04:42,062
And what do you get, besides plants?

59
00:04:42,463 --> 00:04:47,260
I get a wall. For nine years I have been the only
person in my service who understands

60
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:52,189
that you cannot be contained, and the pressure on me
to attempt it increases every year.

61
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:57,119
Lyon made it much worse; there are four men in my
building who now want a Chinese Tyrant

62
00:04:57,139 --> 00:05:02,216
and believe we can steal the method. They cannot, and
the attempt would end with my country

63
00:05:02,236 --> 00:05:07,033
in a confrontation it would lose in a way it would
never be able to explain to its own

64
00:05:07,053 --> 00:05:07,425
people.

65
00:05:07,704 --> 00:05:12,314
So I will buy nine years of peace with a
factory. That is the whole of it.

66
00:05:13,154 --> 00:05:15,204
You have left something out.

67
00:05:15,605 --> 00:05:16,566
Yes.

68
00:05:16,966 --> 00:05:17,724
Say it.

69
00:05:18,124 --> 00:05:23,004
If you ever use one of those things on our soil, or
against our people, or if a single

70
00:05:23,024 --> 00:05:27,905
human being in this country is harmed by anything of
yours — I will spend every hour I

71
00:05:27,925 --> 00:05:32,863
have left proving what you are to the entire world,
with evidence, whatever it costs me

72
00:05:32,883 --> 00:05:37,991
and whatever it costs my service. I will not be able
to stop you. I am telling you plainly

73
00:05:38,011 --> 00:05:41,353
that I will make the next thirty years
extremely expensive.

74
00:05:41,754 --> 00:05:47,440
And Albert Wesker turned his head and looked at her
for a long moment, and the narrator

75
00:05:47,460 --> 00:05:52,754
would like to be clear about what he felt, which
was neither anger nor amusement.

76
00:05:53,153 --> 00:05:54,283
It was relief.

77
00:05:54,803 --> 00:06:01,334
Director Wen, do you know how long I have been
waiting for somebody to say that to me?

78
00:06:01,733 --> 00:06:03,704
Ten years, I should think.

79
00:06:04,103 --> 00:06:11,663
Twenty-nine. Accepted, on one condition of my own.
When a provincial official does become

80
00:06:11,683 --> 00:06:19,157
curious, you will not transfer him. You will send him
to me, and I will offer him a job,

81
00:06:19,177 --> 00:06:25,033
and if he refuses it he goes back to his
post with his career intact.

82
00:06:25,434 --> 00:06:26,353
Why?

83
00:06:26,752 --> 00:06:32,937
Because the people who notice are the only ones
worth having, and because in ten years

84
00:06:32,957 --> 00:06:39,502
I have found that if you do not collect them, somebody
eventually turns them into a martyr.

85
00:06:39,903 --> 00:06:41,153
She considered that.

86
00:06:41,673 --> 00:06:46,864
You have just told me how you handle every person
who gets close to you. I do not think

87
00:06:46,884 --> 00:06:47,643
you meant to.

88
00:06:48,043 --> 00:06:49,193
I meant to.

89
00:06:49,593 --> 00:06:55,159
Wen Shulan went back to her office after the park
and wrote the assessment that got her

90
00:06:55,179 --> 00:07:00,553
the eleven years, and the narrator has it, and it
is not what her ministry expected.

91
00:07:01,072 --> 00:07:06,283
He offered me one thing I did not ask for and I have
been thinking about it for a week.

92
00:07:06,562 --> 00:07:12,044
I told him that curious officials would be
transferred. He asked me instead to send them

93
00:07:12,064 --> 00:07:17,609
to him, so that he could offer them employment, and
said that if they refused they should

94
00:07:17,629 --> 00:07:20,673
go back to their posts with their
careers intact.

95
00:07:20,952 --> 00:07:26,099
(very slow) My first reading was that he wishes to
collect our people. That reading is

96
00:07:26,119 --> 00:07:28,622
wrong and it took me four days to see why.

97
00:07:28,903 --> 00:07:34,573
Consider what he actually asked for: that the people
in this service who are clever enough

98
00:07:34,593 --> 00:07:40,011
to notice him should not be punished for noticing.
He has protected them from *me*. He

99
00:07:40,031 --> 00:07:45,701
has made it safer, inside the Ministry of State
Security, to be right about Albert Wesker.

100
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:51,399
In nine years those officers will be senior. Every
one of them will owe their career to

101
00:07:51,419 --> 00:07:55,151
a rule he asked for. Not one of them
will have taken a coin.

102
00:07:55,870 --> 00:08:01,557
(very slow) I have read four thousand recruitment
operations. I have never seen one conducted

103
00:08:01,577 --> 00:08:05,300
by asking the target's employer to stop
firing the good ones.

104
00:08:05,581 --> 00:08:10,904
Recommendation unchanged: build the wall. But
record, so that whoever holds this desk

105
00:08:10,924 --> 00:08:16,248
in twenty years knows it, that the wall is not to
keep him out. It is to keep our own

106
00:08:16,268 --> 00:08:21,655
best people from walking towards him, and it will
not work, and I do not have a better

107
00:08:21,675 --> 00:08:21,969
idea.

108
00:08:22,370 --> 00:08:24,790
Umbrella built in China the slow way.

109
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:31,375
Three plants and a research campus at Suzhou, four
hundred and eleven hectares, thirty-one

110
00:08:31,395 --> 00:08:37,442
thousand employees, every one of them hired through
advertisements and interviews, every

111
00:08:37,462 --> 00:08:43,991
building erected over thirty-eight months by Chinese
contractors in front of Chinese inspectors

112
00:08:44,011 --> 00:08:45,300
with Chinese steel.

113
00:08:45,701 --> 00:08:52,468
It cost nineteen billion dollars and four years and
it was, by a considerable margin,

114
00:08:52,488 --> 00:08:56,381
the least efficient thing Albert
Wesker ever did.

115
00:08:56,780 --> 00:09:02,723
It was also the most valuable, and the narrator will
explain why in one sentence: it is

116
00:09:02,743 --> 00:09:08,617
the only large piece of Umbrella on this planet
whose existence nobody has ever had to

117
00:09:08,637 --> 00:09:14,854
explain, and for the next fifty years, whenever anyone
anywhere asked whether the company's

118
00:09:14,874 --> 00:09:20,954
buildings were real, somebody produced a photograph
of the Suzhou site under construction

119
00:09:20,974 --> 00:09:21,503
in 2037.

120
00:09:22,022 --> 00:09:23,699
You could have placed it in a night.

121
00:09:24,099 --> 00:09:24,989
Yes.

122
00:09:25,389 --> 00:09:26,939
You're building an alibi.

123
00:09:27,339 --> 00:09:34,113
I am building a *photograph*. In eleven years
somebody in a parliament is going to hold

124
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:40,907
up a picture of the Newark plant and ask how it was
built, and Pell is going to hold up

125
00:09:40,927 --> 00:09:47,702
a picture of Suzhou with a crane in it, and the room
will settle, because a room always

126
00:09:47,722 --> 00:09:51,529
settles when it is given
something it recognises.

127
00:09:51,928 --> 00:09:57,514
And there was a second reason, which he told nobody
and which the narrator has only from

128
00:09:57,534 --> 00:09:58,788
the System's ledger.

129
00:09:59,938 --> 00:10:07,163
Note. The Suzhou territory was not placed, not
integrated, and no memory was adjusted.

130
00:10:07,183 --> 00:10:14,576
Points from this facility are earned at the ordinary
rate, from labour and revenue only.

131
00:10:14,596 --> 00:10:20,977
Observation: this is the first thing you have
built that I did not give you.

132
00:10:21,567 --> 00:10:23,097
Was that a criticism?

133
00:10:23,498 --> 00:10:25,163
It was an observation.

134
00:10:25,563 --> 00:10:32,817
It was a criticism. Note this in return: in 2026 you
gave me a building, eleven people

135
00:10:32,837 --> 00:10:40,345
and a mission, and the mission said *fifty staff*. It
did not say *build*. You have spent

136
00:10:40,365 --> 00:10:47,534
ten years teaching me to buy, and I have decided
that a man who can only buy is a man

137
00:10:47,554 --> 00:10:49,734
with exactly one supplier.

138
00:10:50,519 --> 00:10:51,808
(flat) Noted.

139
00:10:52,208 --> 00:10:58,257
The narrator asks you to file that exchange away. It
is 2036. There are fifty-five years

140
00:10:58,277 --> 00:11:04,119
left in this account, and that is the first
sentence in it that points at the ending.

141
00:11:04,519 --> 00:11:10,853
Wen Shulan kept her side of it for eleven years, and
she did it against increasing pressure,

142
00:11:10,873 --> 00:11:13,408
and twice it nearly cost her the job.

143
00:11:13,808 --> 00:11:19,978
She and Wesker met four more times: in 2039, in
2044, in 2047 and once more at the very

144
00:11:19,998 --> 00:11:26,026
end, in circumstances neither of them could have
imagined on a park bench. They never

145
00:11:26,046 --> 00:11:32,713
became friends. She never stopped watching him, and he
never stopped knowing she was watching,

146
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:38,832
and both of them considered the arrangement the most
honest relationship they had with

147
00:11:38,852 --> 00:11:41,606
anyone outside their own organisations.

148
00:11:42,006 --> 00:11:48,503
On the last night of 2039 she wrote her annual
assessment, as she had every year since

149
00:11:48,523 --> 00:11:55,171
2028, and the narrator has it, because it was
declassified in 2071 and because it is the

150
00:11:55,191 --> 00:12:00,626
single best contemporary description of what
was happening to the world.

151
00:12:01,147 --> 00:12:06,881
The subject has not lied to me in four years. The
subject has not broken a single term

152
00:12:06,901 --> 00:12:12,702
of our understanding. The subject has, in that
period, saved approximately five million

153
00:12:12,722 --> 00:12:18,658
lives by ordinary commercial means and has never once
asked this government for anything.

154
00:12:18,937 --> 00:12:25,010
It is my assessment that he is not our enemy, that
he has no intention of becoming our

155
00:12:25,030 --> 00:12:28,128
enemy, and that this is
entirely irrelevant.

156
00:12:28,408 --> 00:12:33,697
A man who can do what he can do, and who answers to
nobody, is a permanent condition of

157
00:12:33,717 --> 00:12:38,945
the world now — like weather, or the sea. We do not
have a policy for the sea. We have

158
00:12:38,965 --> 00:12:39,677
engineering.

159
00:12:39,957 --> 00:12:45,571
Recommendation: continue the arrangement. Build the
wall higher. And begin, quietly, to

160
00:12:45,591 --> 00:12:51,528
consider what this country will do in the year that he
decides he is finished being patient.

161
00:12:51,927 --> 00:12:55,577
She was right about that too. It took
him seven more years.
